 for 77 homeless veterans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134673874.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jon Bon Jovi’s Soul Foundation backed a housing project at the former Walter Reed Army Medical Center in Washington, DC. The development opened in 2019 with 77 permanent supportive housing units for formerly homeless veterans. The project was part of a wider redevelopment of the former 66-acre military medical centre.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jon-bon-jovis-foundation-helped-turn-part-of-the-former-walter-reed-army-medical-center-into-housing-in-2019-the-washington-project-opened-with-homes-for-77-formerly-homeless-veterans/articleshow/134673874.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jon-bon-jovis-foundation-helped-turn-part-of-the-former-walter-reed-army-medical-center-into-housing-in-2019-the-washington-project-opened-with-homes-for-77-formerly-homeless-veterans/articleshow/134673874.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T22:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134674090,imgsize-82146.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[300+ objections as Maidstone residents oppose former hotel conversion into 42 studios for 65 people]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134677426.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[More than 300 objections have been filed against plans to convert Maidstone’s former Grange Moor Hotel into 42 studio apartments for an estimated 65 people. Residents say they are concerned the development could increase pressure on parking, local infrastructure and the neighbourhood, with some describing themselves as “devastated” and saying they would not have bought their homes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/more-than-300-objections-filed-as-maidstone-residents-oppose-plans-to-convert-former-grange-moor-hotel-into-42-studio-apartments-for-65-people-warning-of-added-pressure-on-parking-and-infrastructure/articleshow/134677426.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/more-than-300-objections-filed-as-maidstone-residents-oppose-plans-to-convert-former-grange-moor-hotel-into-42-studio-apartments-for-65-people-warning-of-added-pressure-on-parking-and-infrastructure/articleshow/134677426.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T21:16:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134677440,imgsize-149204.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Baltimore shooting: 12-year-old girl killed in crossfire after parking dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134677289.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/baltimore-shooting-12-year-old-girl-killed-in-crossfire-after-parking-dispute/articleshow/134677289.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/baltimore-shooting-12-year-old-girl-killed-in-crossfire-after-parking-dispute/articleshow/134677289.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T21:29:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134677668,imgsize-154674.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cornell sexual assault case: Woman at centre of rape allegations got threats to withdraw lawsuit, lawyer says]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134677417.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cornell-sexual-assault-case-woman-at-centre-of-rape-allegations-got-threats-to-withdraw-lawsuit-lawyer-says/articleshow/134677417.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cornell-sexual-assault-case-woman-at-centre-of-rape-allegations-got-threats-to-withdraw-lawsuit-lawyer-says/articleshow/134677417.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T21:23:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134677588,imgsize-301568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas landowners feared border wall would cut off Rio Grande access; judge blocks Big Bend construction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134676172.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant ruling, a federal judge has temporarily halted the construction of border barriers in Texas' Big Bend area. Local landowners and environmental advocates express concerns about restricted access to the Rio Grande, claiming the barriers would disrupt the ecosystem and infringe on constitutional rights. The federal government asserts that security measures necessitate these barriers. This decision has sparked six lawsuits contesting the planned border initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-landowners-feared-border-barriers-would-cut-off-access-to-the-rio-grande-an-october-2-court-order-now-blocks-construction-in-the-big-bend-sector-while-the-legal-challenge-continues/articleshow/134676172.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-landowners-feared-border-barriers-would-cut-off-access-to-the-rio-grande-an-october-2-court-order-now-blocks-construction-in-the-big-bend-sector-while-the-legal-challenge-continues/articleshow/134676172.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T20:28:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134676973,imgsize-1793792.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Donald Trump’s climate cuts left thousands jobless; Climate Reserve created a lifeline for 50 experts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134676542.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Donald Trump’s second-term climate cuts scrapped billions in research funding and left thousands of federal workers jobless. In response, climate experts launched Climate Reserve, a multimillion-dollar initiative helping displaced scientists find new roles and revive disrupted projects. The group expected to place 50 experts in new positions while preserving critical climate research and expertise.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-donald-trumps-second-term-climate-cuts-scrapped-billions-in-research-grants-and-left-thousands-of-federal-workers-jobless-climate-reserve-stepped-in-with-new-roles-for-50-climate-experts/articleshow/134676542.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-donald-trumps-second-term-climate-cuts-scrapped-billions-in-research-grants-and-left-thousands-of-federal-workers-jobless-climate-reserve-stepped-in-with-new-roles-for-50-climate-experts/articleshow/134676542.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T19:59:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134676685,imgsize-110660.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[He paid $30 for a painting that sold for $1.35 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134676403.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At a recent estate sale, a man bought a Gertrude Abercrombie painting for only $30. Upon confirming its authenticity at an exhibition, he opted to auction the piece. Titled Alderman Merriam's Shells, the painting was anticipated to sell between $150,000 and $250,000. Remarkably, it sold for a staggering $1,060,000 at Freeman's auction, setting a new high for the artist and highlighting the incredible value of art investments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-collector-paid-30-for-a-seashell-painting-at-an-estate-sale-it-was-later-identified-as-a-1951-gertrude-abercrombie-work-now-it-has-sold-in-new-york-for-a-record-1352600/articleshow/134676403.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-collector-paid-30-for-a-seashell-painting-at-an-estate-sale-it-was-later-identified-as-a-1951-gertrude-abercrombie-work-now-it-has-sold-in-new-york-for-a-record-1352600/articleshow/134676403.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T19:45:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134676496,imgsize-337237.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: Massive fire at Saudi Aramco sites targeted in Houthi missile, drone strikes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134675822.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/watch-massive-fire-at-saudi-aramco-sites-targeted-in-houthi-missile-drone-strikes/articleshow/134675822.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/watch-massive-fire-at-saudi-aramco-sites-targeted-in-houthi-missile-drone-strikes/articleshow/134675822.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T19:34:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134676345,imgsize-11843136.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From India to Australia: How 6 countries got caught up in flydubai terror]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134675881.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On September 30, the flydubai Flight FZ1073 faced a cockpit attack when Omani co-pilot Hammam al-Hammami stabbed Captain Smit Machchhar. The injured pilot bravely opened the cockpit door, allowing crew and passengers to subdue the co-pilot. The flight was diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, where al-Hammami was apprehended by authorities. Investigations have since been undertaken by several countries into al-Hammami’s background and possible extremist ties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/india-uae-saudi-israel-oman-and-australia-how-6-countries-got-caught-up-in-flydubai-terror/articleshow/134675881.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/india-uae-saudi-israel-oman-and-australia-how-6-countries-got-caught-up-in-flydubai-terror/articleshow/134675881.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T19:26:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134676254,imgsize-93712.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Retired FBI agent’s decade-long mission to rediscover 30 ‘lost’ apple varieties]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134675678.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2012, retired FBI agent Dave Benscoter began searching for forgotten apple varieties after discovering unidentified trees in a churchgoer’s orchard. What started as curiosity became a decade-long mission. Alongside fellow apple enthusiasts, Benscoter has helped rediscover 30 once-lost varieties while preserving historic apple trees across the Pacific Northwest for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-a-retired-fbi-agent-began-searching-for-lost-apples-more-than-a-decade-later-his-mission-has-helped-rediscover-30-forgotten-varieties-across-the-pacific-northwest/articleshow/134675678.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-a-retired-fbi-agent-began-searching-for-lost-apples-more-than-a-decade-later-his-mission-has-helped-rediscover-30-forgotten-varieties-across-the-pacific-northwest/articleshow/134675678.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T18:47:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134675810,imgsize-211182.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US man convicted of killing motorist to be resentenced after court rejects AI video of victim forgiving him]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134675493.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-man-convicted-of-killing-motorist-to-be-resentenced-after-court-rejects-ai-video-of-victim-forgiving-him/articleshow/134675493.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-man-convicted-of-killing-motorist-to-be-resentenced-after-court-rejects-ai-video-of-victim-forgiving-him/articleshow/134675493.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T18:42:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure 