 a valuation of $500,000. The artwork depicts early Laguna Beach and showcases Kleitsch's significant contributions to California Impressionism. Following its appearance on Antiques Roadshow, the painting sold for an undisclosed amount exceeding the television valuation. It subsequently featured in exhibitions at the Irvine Museum and Laguna Art Museum in later years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1939-a-california-family-bought-a-joseph-kleitsch-painting-from-his-widow-for-100-75-years-later-their-daughter-brought-it-to-antiques-roadshow-and-heard-a-500000-valuation/articleshow/134655272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1939-a-california-family-bought-a-joseph-kleitsch-painting-from-his-widow-for-100-75-years-later-their-daughter-brought-it-to-antiques-roadshow-and-heard-a-500000-valuation/articleshow/134655272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T16:58:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134655308,imgsize-1020459.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Leonardo DiCaprio gave $1 million to a Seychelles debt swap that protected 410,000 sq km of ocean]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134673582.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Seychelles protected 30% of its ocean by 2020 through a debt conversion deal linked to long-term conservation. The plan safeguards 410,000 sq km of ocean, while allowing sustainable fishing, tourism and other economic activities. Leonardo DiCaprio Foundation was among the private funders supporting the financial transaction.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/leonardo-dicaprios-foundation-gave-1-million-to-a-seychelles-debt-swap-deal-by-2020-the-wider-project-had-helped-the-island-nation-protect-410000-sq-km-of-ocean-an-area-larger-than-germany/articleshow/134673582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/leonardo-dicaprios-foundation-gave-1-million-to-a-seychelles-debt-swap-deal-by-2020-the-wider-project-had-helped-the-island-nation-protect-410000-sq-km-of-ocean-an-area-larger-than-germany/articleshow/134673582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134673818,imgsize-51782.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Astronomers spot gas falling onto a neutron star, revealing how matter reaches its surface]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134594156.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On February 1, 2025, a research team used the XRISM telescope to study GX 301–2. They captured a unique event of gas falling onto a neutron star. The observations revealed changes in iron absorption lines from redshift to emission over time. The study suggests multi-phase accretion and indicates interactions with the stellar wind. These findings provide new insights into how neutron stars feed on surrounding matter.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/astronomers-spot-gas-falling-onto-a-neutron-star-for-the-first-time-revealing-how-matter-flows-towards-the-star/articleshow/134594156.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/astronomers-spot-gas-falling-onto-a-neutron-star-for-the-first-time-revealing-how-matter-flows-towards-the-star/articleshow/134594156.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134594251,imgsize-1337675.cms"/></item></channel></rss>